# player-flame.px - engine plume for each player nacelle
# canvas 8x12, 2 frames (flicker pair, loop). Plume points down; top row attaches under the nozzle.
# anchor: frame centre (4,6); plume axis x=4.0 (pixel-edge). Drawn once per nacelle, top edge at the
# nacelle bottom (player y=+14 from centre), centred on x=-5 and x=+5 from the player centre.
# no outline (emissive); fire ramp only, hot core (fire-4) at the root, cooling to fire-1/fire-0 tail.
# light: self-lit. Frame B is longer with a narrower neck so the pair reads as a flicker, not a pulse.
# timing: 50 ms each (3 ticks); the engine may also alternate per frame.
palette
. transparent
F #a8401a  fire-1
O #ffb347  fire-3
f #5c1d12  fire-0
o #ec7424  fire-2
y #fff0b8  fire-4
ramp fire f F o O y
frame a 50
..oOOo..
.oOyyOo.
..OyyO..
..oOOo..
...OO...
...oo...
...Fo...
...FF...
...F....
...f....
........
........
frame b 50
..oOOo..
..OyyO..
..OyyO..
..OyyO..
..oOOo..
...OO...
...oo...
...oo...
...oF...
...FF...
....F...
....f...
